    help: 🎛️ Team instructions. Four sit beside the mentality on the Tactics tab: pressing, tempo, width and the defensive line, each on balanced or pushed one way or the other. Balanced on all four is the game exactly as it always played. Everything else buys you something and charges you for it. What each one costs. A high press wins the ball in their half and makes chances early, but it tires the side: more goals against late on, more knocks, and 5 fitness off every man who played. A direct side goes straight over it. A high line squeezes the pitch and catches them offside, and leaves space behind. Direct tempo gives the ball away for better chances, patient play keeps it and takes more, worse shots. Going wide gets crosses in and suits wingers and attacking full backs, and leaves the middle thinner. Read the other dugout. Every club plays a style, and the match preview names it with a line on
